CORE
main.c
--unwind 3
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^Repeating symbolic execution
--
The threads write values to shared objects (the mutex model's fields, and
__CPROVER_dead_object when main's locals die) that the first run did not have,
but no lookup by another thread lacked them: main writes the latter after all
its lookups. Repeating symbolic execution is not needed, and is skipped.
